<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="1536"
    android:viewportHeight="1536">
    <!--
        Themed-icon (monochrome) layer.

        The launcher tints this with a single colour taken from the user's wallpaper, so it has to
        be a flat silhouette — the gradient that makes the colour icon recognisable carries no
        information once it is reduced to one tint. For a solid sphere the honest silhouette is
        just the filled circle.

        Viewport 1536×1536 maps to 108dp. Radius 630 centred at (768,768) is a 1260-unit diameter,
        i.e. 82% of the canvas — deliberately larger than the 72dp safe zone so the launcher's
        circular mask cuts through solid shape rather than along the art's antialiased edge, which
        is what produced a faint dark ring. Matches the raster foreground exactly.

        Two 180° arcs rather than one 360° arc: an SVG/vector elliptical arc whose start and end
        points are identical is degenerate and renders as nothing.
    -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M138,768 A630,630 0 0,1 1398,768 A630,630 0 0,1 138,768 Z" />
</vector>
